---
layout: layout.njk
permalink: /search/
title: Search
description: Search everything I’ve built, and narrow it by status, the year it started, topic, collection, and language.
---
{#- Search and facets. The page lists every thing, as the index does, so it works without JavaScript.
    site/js/search.js loads the Pagefind index (collection/search-index.ts) for the words, then narrows and
    orders this list by the facet values each row carries, adds the passage that matched, and keeps the query
    and filters in the address. The values and their counts come from the model (collection/site.ts); the
    script updates the counts as the list narrows. #}
<section class="intro search-intro">
  <h1 class="title">Search what I’ve <span class="accent">built</span><span class="dot">.</span></h1>
  <form class="search-form" role="search" action="/search/" data-search-form hidden>
    <label class="search-label" for="search-query">Search the words of every thing, or narrow the list with the filters.</label>
    <div class="search-row">
      <input id="search-query" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="A wiki, a bot, a newsletter, Clash Royale" data-search-query />
      <button type="button" class="surprise" data-search-surprise>Surprise me</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
<div class="search-layout" data-search>
  <details class="facet-panel" data-search-facets hidden>
    <summary>Filters<span class="selected" data-search-selected></span></summary>
    {% for facet in site.facets %}
    <fieldset class="facet facet-{{ facet.name }}" data-facet="{{ facet.name }}">
      <legend>{{ facet.label }}</legend>
      {% if facet.name == 'year' %}
      <div class="histogram" style="--most: {{ facet.most }}">
        {% for v in facet.values %}
        <span class="year">
          {% if v.count %}<button type="button" class="bar" data-value="{{ v.value }}" data-label="{{ v.label }}" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Started {{ v.label }}, {{ v.count }} thing{{ "s" if v.count != 1 }}" title="{{ v.label }}: {{ v.count }} thing{{ "s" if v.count != 1 }}" style="--total: {{ v.count }}; --n: {{ v.count }}"><span class="fill"></span></button>{% else %}<span class="bar empty"></span>{% endif %}
          {% if v.value | int % 5 == 0 %}<span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">{{ v.label }}</span>{% endif %}
        </span>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <p class="chips">
        {% for v in facet.values %}<button type="button" class="chip{% if facet.name == 'status' %} status status-{{ v.value }}{% endif %}" data-value="{{ v.value }}" data-label="{{ v.label }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ v.label }}<span class="count" data-count>{{ v.count }}</span></button> {% endfor %}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
    </fieldset>
    {% endfor %}
    <p class="facet-note muted">Written in is the top language GitHub reports for each repository.</p>
  </details>
  <div class="search-results">
    <div class="search-bar">
      <p class="search-status"><span role="status" data-search-status>Search needs JavaScript. Every thing I’ve built is listed below.</span> <button type="button" class="clear" data-search-clear hidden>Clear</button></p>
      <label class="sort" data-search-sort-label hidden>Sort
        <select data-search-sort>
          <option value="match">Best match</option>
          <option value="title">A to Z</option>
          <option value="newest">Newest first</option>
          <option value="oldest">Oldest first</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <ol class="thing-list" data-search-results>
      {% for thing in site.things %}{% include "thing-row.njk" %}{% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>
<script type="module" src="{{ assets.search }}"></script>
